<section class="phero"><div class="phero-media"><img src="/assets/img/photos/chesapeake-waterway.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/chesapeake-waterway-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/chesapeake-waterway.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="800" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.18"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/virginia-localities/">Localities</a><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Chesapeake</span></nav><p class="kicker">Hampton Roads</p><h1>Insurance Appraiser in Chesapeake, VA</h1><p class="lede">Chesapeake is one of the largest cities by land area in Virginia, part suburb and part farm country. Its claims range from subdivision roofs to barns and pole buildings.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-accent" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="i" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost-light" href="/schedule-a-claim-review/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="hero-facts"><div><dt>Locality</dt><dd>Independent city (no county)</dd></div><div><dt>Region</dt><dd>Hampton Roads</dd></div><div><dt>Inspections</dt><dd>On site</dd></div></dl></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose"><div class="note"><b class="h">Local claim risks</b><ul class="chips chips-dark"><li>Hurricane wind</li><li>Fallen pines</li><li>Hail</li><li>Crawlspace water</li><li>Tornadoes</li></ul><p class="note-small"><b>Housing mix:</b> Suburban subdivisions on crawlspaces, rural homes and farm buildings, newer townhomes.</p></div>
<h2>A city that’s also countryside</h2>
<p>Chesapeake covers about 350 square miles, from the shopping centers of Greenbrier to the farm fields of Hickory and the edge of the Great Dismal Swamp. The Albemarle and Chesapeake Canal and the Intracoastal Waterway run through it. That mix produces a wide range of claims: subdivision roofs in Great Bridge and Grassfield, waterfront homes along the Elizabeth River in Western Branch and Deep Creek, and agricultural buildings in the southern part of the city.</p>
<h2>Storms that shaped Chesapeake claims</h2>
<p>Hurricane Isabel in 2003 brought down thousands of loblolly pines across the city. Shallow-rooted pines in saturated soil remain one of the most common causes of roof damage here. Tropical storm remnants and summer squall lines bring wind and occasional tornadoes, and spring hail hits the newer subdivisions where nearly every roof is the same age.</p>
<h2>What Chesapeake owners bring us</h2>
<ul>
<li>Pine trees through roofs, with disputes over crane removal and framing repair.</li>
<li>Whole-subdivision hail claims where the insurer pays for a few slopes.</li>
<li>Crawlspace water losses with wet subfloors, insulation and ductwork.</li>
<li>Outbuildings, pole barns and fences under Other Structures limits.</li>
<li>Vinyl siding that can’t be matched after wind damage to one elevation.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Housing mix</h2>
<p>Most homes date from the 1980s onward: two-story vinyl-sided colonials, ranches and townhomes on crawlspaces, with custom homes on larger lots. Older homes sit in South Norfolk, one of Chesapeake’s historic neighborhoods, with early-1900s frame houses and brick churches.</p>
<h2>Services available in Chesapeake</h2><p>Every Virginia Insurance Appraiser service is available to property owners in Chesapeake and the surrounding area, including:</p><ul class="cols2"><li><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/appraisal-demand-representation/">Appraisal Clause Representation</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/homeowners-insurance-appraisal/">Homeowners Insurance Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/commercial-and-hoa-claim-appraisal/">Commercial &amp; HOA Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/hail-and-roof-damage-appraisal/">Roof &amp; Hail Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/windstorm-and-tornado-appraisal/">Wind &amp; Tornado Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/hurricane-and-noreaster-appraisal/">Hurricane &amp; Nor’easter Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/water-damage-claim-appraisal/">Water Damage Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-and-umpire-services/fire-and-smoke-damage-appraisal/">Fire &amp; Smoke Damage Appraisal</a></li></ul><h2>Questions from Chesapeake property owners</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>A pine fell on my house and the estimate only covers the roof. Is that normal?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Often not. Tree strikes can crack rafters, damage interior ceilings and require crane work. Those items belong in the dwelling repair when the policy covers the loss.</p></div></details><details><summary>Are barns covered under my homeowners policy?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Detached structures are usually covered under Other Structures, typically 10% of the dwelling limit, unless they’re used for business or farming, which may need separate coverage.</p></div></details></div><h2>Nearby localities</h2><div class="related"><a href="/virginia-localities/insurance-appraiser-virginia-beach-va/"><small>Nearby</small><span>Virginia Beach</span><